      <workList xml:id="workDesc_ad6e3ba0">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e225222">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_bb3a4b25">B2:410</identifier>
            <title xml:id="_19" xml:lang="da">Cantate i Anledning af Kong Christian den Syvendes Fødsels Dag</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_838ad312">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="_21">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
               <persName role="author" xml:id="_23">Benjamin Georg Sporon</persName>
               <persName role="dedicatee" xml:id="_22">King Christian VII</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_24_0">
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_385370e3">Copenhagen</geogName>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_24_0">
               <p xml:id="idm117">Only the text book to the birthday cantata for <persName xml:id="idm118" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Christian VII</persName> seems to have survived. Since Scheibe died in 1776 the work must have been composed for a celebration at the latest that year. However, that seems rather unlikely since the indication on title page, ‘Musik er af Capelmester Scheibe, hvortil poesien er sat af Assessor <persName xml:id="idm119" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" auth="VIAF" role="">Sporon</persName>’ (‘Music by Kapellmeister Scheibe to which the poetry has been added by assessor Sporon’), strongly suggests that the poet took one of Scheibe’s cantatas and simply replaced the original text with a new one which was then performed at The Musical Academy in 1778. A couple of weeks later the complete text was published in the newspaper <rend xml:id="idm120" fontstyle="italic">Kiøbenhavns Adresse-Contoirs Efterretninger</rend>.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_5f7e2b15">
               <language xml:id="da">Danish</language>
            </langUsage>
            <biblList xml:id="listBibl_a21afff6-f527-41be-835a-f4147e4a9159269">
